  {"name":"Astra Microwave Products Limited","sym":"ASTRAMICRO","q":"Q2 FY27","date":"13 Nov 2026","tone":"Optimistic","guidance":"Revenue growth of approximately 15%, targeting INR1,300–1,350 crores for FY27; EBITDA margin 26%–28%; newly stated on this call.","gchange":{"m":"Revenue","was":"","now":"Approximately 15% growth; INR1,300–1,350 crores","ch":"New"},"ggrowth":"Approximately 15%","gbase":null,"yoy":"","metrics":[{"m":"H1 FY27 revenue","v":"INR437 crores"},{"m":"H1 FY27 EBITDA","v":"INR120 crores"},{"m":"H1 FY27 EBITDA margin","v":"27.4%"},{"m":"H1 FY27 PAT","v":"INR57 crores"},{"m":"H1 FY27 PAT margin","v":"13%"},{"m":"Uttam AAAU order","v":"INR1,844 crores from HAL"},{"m":"Standalone order book","v":"INR3,937 crores as of 30 September 2026"},{"m":"Consolidated order book","v":"INR4,708 crores as of 30 September 2026"},{"m":"Service orders in consolidated book","v":"INR251 crores"},{"m":"Q2 FY27 order inflow","v":"INR2,036 crores"},{"m":"Radar order inflow","v":"INR1,967 crores"},{"m":"Electronic warfare order inflow","v":"INR36 crores"},{"m":"Telemetry order inflow","v":"INR17 crores"},{"m":"Space order inflow","v":"INR16 crores"},{"m":"ARC H1 orders","v":"INR413 crores"},{"m":"ARC H1 sales","v":"INR334 crores"},{"m":"ASTL order book","v":"Around INR900 crores"},{"m":"ASTL weather inquiry pipeline","v":"Around INR2,000 crores"},{"m":"ISRO remote-sensing payload share","v":"Estimated 30%–40% of hardware"},{"m":"ISRO communication payload share","v":"Nearly 25%–35% of hardware"}],"takeaways":["FY27 revenue guidance: Management guided for approximately 15% top-line growth, targeting INR1,300–1,350 crores, with EBITDA margin guidance of 26%–28%.","Demerger structure: Astra shareholders are expected to receive one Astra Space Technologies Limited share for every Astra share held, without additional payment, subject to scheme completion.","Defence order visibility: Management reiterated an INR8,000–10,000 crore order base building over coming years, with a substantial part already in hand.","FY29 revenue ambition: Management outlined a path towards INR2,000 crores turnover in FY29, plus or minus INR100 crores, followed by INR2,000–3,000 crores in subsequent years.","Margin guidance: Management said 26%–28% is a comfortable EBITDA margin range for the next two to three years, with possible operating leverage upside."],"revenue":["Production-order mix: Management attributed the H1 performance to favourable product mix led by domestic defence production orders and better operating-expense control.","ARC joint venture: ARC booked INR413 crores of orders and INR334 crores of sales in H1; management described strategic and tactical communications as its business focus.","Space business: ASTL's space and weather activities include space-qualified subsystems, satellite assembly, ground stations, weather radars and forecasting-related services.","Export development: Management reported international customer leads and prototype discussions; qualification and order conversion may take time.","Product opportunities: Management cited bird-detection radar, low-level lightweight radar and counter-drone systems as three company-developed products."],"profit":["Margin drivers: Management attributed higher margins to a favourable production-order mix; it said quarterly margins can vary with product mix.","Operating leverage: Management expects much of the incremental business to flow to the bottom line because it does not expect the fixed-cost base to increase dramatically.","Working-capital target: Management is working to reduce the cash conversion cycle to around 350 days by year-end, while acknowledging geopolitical and supply-chain issues.","Inventory build-up: Management said inventory was accumulated for components with longer delivery lead times to protect deliveries, including the first quarter of the next financial year.","Debt reduction: Management said it is targeting near debt-free status over the next one to one-and-a-half years; the CFO also said working-capital limits are targeted to reach zero by year-end."],"pipeline":["Counter-drone delivery: The counter-drone radar was delivered to DRDO for final integration and trials; management said the complete solution had also been demonstrated to customers.","Radar development: Small and medium-range surveillance radars, next-generation RF seekers, broadband jammers and ammunition electronics were in advanced development stages, with field trials expected from next quarter.","Electronic mines: Management said it was developing a new-age electronic mines product and expected to discuss it before year-end.","Space demerger: ASTL is being positioned as a separate space and weather business; the proposed shareholder entitlement is one ASTL share for every Astra share.","R&D and production: Management said it would continue investing in R&D and production capabilities.","Global product development: Management described a shift from supplying subsystems to developing complete systems with Astra-owned IP and in-house digital signal and radar-data processing."],"commitments":[{"c":"FY27 revenue","s":"Approximately 15% top-line growth; target INR1,300–1,350 crores","t":"FY27","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"EBITDA margin","s":"Steady-state EBITDA margin of 26%–28%","t":"Next two to three years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"FY29 turnover","s":"INR2,000 crores, plus or minus INR100 crores","t":"FY29","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Later turnover","s":"INR2,000–3,000 crores","t":"A few years thereafter","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Debt position","s":"Near debt-free status","t":"Next one to one-and-a-half years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"ASTL shareholder entitlement","s":"One ASTL share for every Astra share held, without additional payment","t":"When the scheme is complete","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"ASTL cumulative revenue","s":"INR2,250–2,500 crores","t":"Next four years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"ASTL annual revenue","s":"Around INR800–900 crores","t":"FY31","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"ASTL weather pipeline","s":"Weather inquiry pipeline of around INR2,000 crores","t":"No date","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Electronic mines","s":"Management said it would discuss the product before year-end","t":"Before the end of the year","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Bird-detection radar","s":"Expected business of around INR200–300 crores","t":"Next two to three years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Low-level lightweight radar","s":"Visibility of at least around INR1,000 crores","t":"Next five years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Counter-drone market","s":"Management projected an overall market of INR3,000–5,000 crores and hoped to secure at least 30% of the market opened up","t":"Next five years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Cash conversion cycle","s":"Around 350 days","t":"By year-end","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Free cash flow","s":"Somewhere between INR250–350 crores; management said it could not give an exact number","t":"FY27","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Working-capital limits","s":"Management expects working-capital limits to become zero","t":"By year-end","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Uttam AAAU deliveries","s":"Two numbers committed; four numbers being attempted","t":"By March 2027","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Uttam AAAU milestone","s":"12 numbers to be delivered","t":"By March 2028","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Virupaksha radar","s":"Complete 12 numbers","t":"By March 2028","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Virupaksha annual supply","s":"Around 25 units initially, then 33–34 units","t":"FY29 initially; thereafter","st":"Not tracked"}],"ytd":{"st":"Not stated","act":"H1 FY27 revenue INR437 crores","ev":"Management did not explicitly state whether H1 was ahead of or behind FY27 guidance."},"dilution":[],"terms":[{"t":"ASTL","m":"Astra Space Technologies Limited, the proposed separate space and weather business"},{"t":"ARC","m":"Astra's joint venture with Rafael of Israel"},{"t":"AAAU","m":"Uttam AESA airborne radar unit"},{"t":"MMIC","m":"Monolithic microwave integrated circuit"},{"t":"SDR","m":"Software-defined radio"},{"t":"DPM","m":"Defence Procurement Manual"}],"order":{"book":{"v":"Standalone INR3,937 crores; consolidated INR4,708 crores","asof":"30 September 2026","cmp":"Consolidated includes service orders of INR251 crores"},"inflow":{"per":"Q2 FY27","v":"INR2,036 crores","cmp":""},"exec":"Uttam AAAU contract: 12 numbers by March 2028; other contracts have execution cycles of two to three years or four years, as applicable.","pipe":"INR600 crores of orders concluded and expected by next month; management also cited INR200 crores more worth of orders in FY27, but the wording is unclear in the transcript.","base":{"per":"FY26","v":"INR1,163 crores"},"wins":[{"who":"HAL Uttam AAAU","v":"INR1,844 crores","t":"Two numbers committed by March 2027; 12 numbers by March 2028"},{"who":"ARC joint venture","v":"INR413 crores of H1 orders","t":"Management cited further orders of INR1,200–1,500 crores in the next six to eight months"},{"who":"QRSAM","v":"","t":"Main contract expected after BEL receives its contract; execution may start in late FY28 or FY29"},{"who":"Virupaksha radar","v":"","t":"12 numbers by March 2028; around 25 units initially in FY29"}]},"cap":{"util":null,"adds":[{"what":"ASTL weather network installations","cap":"In excess of 1,700 automatic weather stations, radars and wind profilers","start":"Already deployed","capex":"","pot":""},{"what":"Astra's own radar products","cap":"Three products: counter-drone radar, bird-detection radar and low-level lightweight radar","start":"Delivered / demonstrated by Diwali","capex":"","pot":""},{"what":"Electronic mines","cap":"New-age electronic mines product under development","start":"Before the end of the year for further discussion","capex":"","pot":""}],"plan":{"amt":"Continued investment in R&D and production capabilities","per":"Ongoing","fund":""},"turn":""},"decode":{"target":{"m":"Revenue","lo":"INR1,300 crores","hi":"INR1,350 crores","p":"FY27"},"margin":{"m":"EBITDA margin","lo":"26%","hi":"28%","p":""},"capacity":{"v":"Yes","e":"\"Our experienced workforce, engineering talent\" and \"parallel testing infrastructure\"; management also described existing clean rooms and test facilities in the space business."},"orders":{"v":"Yes","e":"\"As of 30th September 2026\" standalone order book INR3,937 crores and consolidated order book INR4,708 crores."},"realism":{"v":"Yes","e":"Management linked margins to production-order mix and operating leverage, and said quarterly margins vary with product mix."}},"risks":"Management cited lengthy customer qualification, competitive bidding, geopolitical supply-chain delays, working-capital intensity and uncertain timing of QRSAM and other large defence orders.","source":"Q2 FY27 earnings-call transcript, 13 Nov 2026: K1–K5 pp2–8; R1–R5 pp2–4, 8–10; P1–P6 pp2–8; C1–C31 pp4–7, 9–18; M1–M20 pp2–4, 6–7, 9–10, 17–18; D1–D5 pp4, 7–10, 14; O1–O4 pp3–4, 10–12, 15–18; U1–U4 pp2–8."},
  {"name":"Azad Engineering Limited","sym":"AZAD","q":"Q2 FY27","date":"7 Nov 2026","tone":"Optimistic","guidance":"FY27 H1 revenue growth of over 25% was exceeded; long-term annual growth guidance reiterated at over 25% plus. FY28 revenue run-rate target newly stated at over INR1,300 crores.","gchange":{"m":"Revenue growth","was":"Earlier guidance of over 25%","now":"Over 25% plus long-term annual growth guidance reiterated","ch":"Maintained"},"ggrowth":"Over 25% plus","gbase":{"per":"H1 FY27","val":"INR358 crores"},"yoy":"31.6%","metrics":[{"m":"Q2 FY27 revenue","v":"INR187.8 crores, +31.6% YoY"},{"m":"Q2 FY27 EBITDA","v":"INR70.4 crores, +37.1% YoY"},{"m":"Q2 FY27 EBITDA margin","v":"37.5%, against 36% a year ago"},{"m":"Q2 FY27 PAT","v":"INR30.8 crores"},{"m":"Q2 FY27 PAT margin","v":"16.4%"},{"m":"H1 FY27 revenue","v":"INR358 crores, +29.3% YoY"},{"m":"H1 FY27 EBITDA","v":"INR134.5 crores, +34.7% YoY"},{"m":"H1 FY27 EBITDA margin","v":"37.5%, against 36% in the same period last year"},{"m":"H1 FY27 PAT","v":"INR67.2 crores, +6.6% YoY"},{"m":"Consolidated H1 revenue","v":"INR363.5 crores"},{"m":"Consolidated H1 EBITDA","v":"INR136.6 crores"},{"m":"Consolidated H1 PAT","v":"INR66.1 crores"},{"m":"Energy and oil and gas H1","v":"INR290 crores, +28.5%"},{"m":"Aerospace and defence H1","v":"INR60.4 crores, +28.3%"},{"m":"Domestic H1 revenue","v":"INR43 crores, more than two and a half times"},{"m":"Q2 export contribution","v":"88% of revenue"},{"m":"H1 export contribution","v":"More than 85% of revenue"},{"m":"Gross margin Q2","v":"INR84.9 crores, 45.2% of revenue"},{"m":"Q2 other income","v":"INR4.7 crores against INR12.7 crores in Q2 FY26"},{"m":"H1 capex","v":"INR139.3 crores"}],"takeaways":["Capacity foundation complete: Management said all six customer-dedicated facilities were commissioned, with production-ready teams, machines, raw material and tooling.","FY28 revenue run-rate: Management expects annual revenue run-rate of over INR1,300 crores by the end of FY28, supported by installed capacity.","Revenue conversion timing: Throughput from new capacity begins in Q3 FY27, revenue ramps from Q4 FY27, and all plants are expected fully ramped by H1 FY28.","Contract visibility clarified: Management said the INR6,500 crore figure is customer demand under contracts over five to seven years, not an order backlog.","Cash-flow transition: Management expects cash generation to improve from Q4 FY27 as throughput converts inventory into finished goods, receivables and cash."],"revenue":["Export-led business: Exports contributed 88% of Q2 revenue; management expects exports to remain about 85% of sales.","Segment mix: H1 energy, oil and gas revenue was INR290 crores; aerospace and defence revenue was INR60.4 crores.","Domestic growth: Domestic revenue grew more than two and a half times to INR43 crores, reaching 12% of business from 6%, helped by BHEL indigenisation work.","Customer concentration: Management said it currently caters to under 2% of customers' wallet share and sees scope to increase share through continuing qualifications.","Aerospace contribution: Management expects energy and oil and gas to represent 55%–60% of revenue by FY2030–31, with the balance from aerospace and defence."],"profit":["Gross-margin drivers: Management attributed gross-margin improvement to operating leverage, local sourcing and backward integration into special processes.","Investment costs: Depreciation increased after INR251 crores of assets were capitalised during H1; employee costs rose because skilled manpower was hired ahead of revenue.","Treasury income: Management said treasury income is moderating as QIP cash is deployed into factory infrastructure and machines.","Working capital: Inventory increased by INR98 crores in H1; INR72 crores was work in progress on new lines awaiting customer approval.","Customer advances: One OEM agreed to provide 50% advance against each purchase order; management expects close to USD4.5 million under this arrangement."],"pipeline":["Dedicated facilities: Six customer-dedicated facilities covering 44,800 square metres were commissioned for Mitsubishi Heavy Industries, GE Vernova, Siemens Energy and Baker Hughes.","Oil and gas ramp-up: The dedicated Baker Hughes oil and gas facility is expected to add a growth lever from Q4 FY27; its supply agreement has been extended to 2030.","Defence engine capability: After delivering India's first indigenous expendable turbojet engine to GTRE, Azad is positioned for end-to-end manufacture, assembly and integration of complete engine assemblies.","Aerospace qualifications: Rolls-Royce, Pratt & Whitney and Safran programmes are progressing; management said production revenue from Rolls-Royce is yet to begin.","Hot-section components: Work has started on hot-section nozzle-vane segments for Mitsubishi Heavy Industries under an eight-year single-source contract.","Future expansion: Management is considering selective acquisitions for large components, full-stack production and co-location with key OEMs."],"commitments":[{"c":"Revenue growth","s":"H1 FY27 growth of over 25% was exceeded; long-term annual growth guidance reiterated at over 25% plus","t":"Long term","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Revenue run-rate","s":"Annual revenue run-rate of over INR1,300 crores","t":"By end of FY28","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Plant ramp-up","s":"All plants expected to be fully ramped up","t":"H1 FY28","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Revenue ramp-up","s":"Revenue expected to start ramping up","t":"Q4 FY27 onwards","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Production throughput","s":"Throughput from new capacity begins","t":"Q3 FY27","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Cash generation","s":"Cash flowing out of the company expected by Q4 end; Q1 next year expected to be \"perfectly in thing\"","t":"Q4 FY27 end; Q1 next year","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Customer advance","s":"One OEM agreed to give 50% advance on each PO; expected close to USD4.5 million","t":"No date","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Bill discounting","s":"ICICI Bank and DP World lines can be used","t":"Q4 FY27 onwards","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Oil and gas facility","s":"Dedicated Baker Hughes facility adds a growth lever","t":"Q4 FY27","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Aero-engine deliveries","s":"Start delivering aero-engine airfoils","t":"Next fiscal onwards","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Qualification batch","s":"Management expects to announce delivery of the first qualification batch","t":"\"Very soon\"","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"New aerospace facilities","s":"Discussions to dedicate one or two remaining Tuniki buildings to aerospace customers; management said it would inform investors \"very soon\"","t":"\"Very soon\"","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"FY29 capex","s":"Plan next phase of capex after current qualifications and customer programmes open up","t":"FY2029 onwards","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Free cash flow","s":"Management expects cash generation to improve as new capacity throughput converts into cash","t":"From Q4 FY27; Q1 next year","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Automation","s":"Management is working to increase automation and use ERP systems to reduce manpower dependency","t":"No date","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Mangampet expansion","s":"Management said Mangampet land is ready for Phase II and that it plans to start there after the current phase","t":"After current phase","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Engine programme","s":"Second engine expected to be delivered; testing ongoing","t":"No date","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Customer programmes","s":"Management expects further Rolls-Royce, Pratt & Whitney and Safran qualifications to add production programmes","t":"Next few years","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Working capital","s":"Management said it is working to bring working capital in check through customer advances and bill discounting","t":"Ongoing","st":"Not tracked"},{"c":"Long-term revenue mix","s":"Energy and oil and gas expected to represent 55%–60% of revenue, with aerospace and defence contributing the balance","t":"FY2030–31","st":"Not tracked"}],"ytd":{"st":"Ahead","act":"H1 FY27 revenue growth 29.3%","ev":"Management said H1 growth was ahead of its 25% guidance."},"dilution":[{"t":"QIP","x":"\"Of the INR700 crores raised through the QIP, INR621.8 crores has been used\"; INR78.2 crores remained in fixed deposit for capex."},{"t":"Other equity raise","x":"Management said further QIP may be considered when required for the next capex phase from FY2029 onwards."}],"terms":[{"t":"Delta qualification","m":"Revalidation when a qualified part moves to a new machine or facility location"},{"t":"OEM","m":"Original equipment manufacturer; the company that makes the final equipment"},{"t":"GTRE","m":"Gas Turbine Research Establishment"},{"t":"Hot section","m":"High-temperature turbine-engine components"},{"t":"ARR","m":"Annual revenue run-rate"},{"t":"QIP","m":"Qualified Institutions Placement, a method of raising equity capital"}],"order":{"book":{"v":"Close to over INR6,500 crores","asof":"As of 7 Nov 2026","cmp":"Management clarified this is not an order backlog; it represents customer demand under contracts over five to seven years."},"inflow":null,"exec":"Customer contracts represent annual demand over five to seven years; new parts and contracts are added over time.","pipe":"Contracts under discussion across segments; management did not quantify the additional pipeline.","base":{"per":"FY26","v":"INR602.975 crores consolidated revenue from operations"},"wins":[{"who":"BHEL","v":"About INR52.68 crores","t":"Two-year rate contract for gas turbine airfoils / blades"},{"who":"Baker Hughes","v":"Supply agreement extended to 2030","t":"Existing agreement"},{"who":"Rolls-Royce","v":"","t":"Eight-year single-source contract for Mitsubishi hot-section nozzle-vane segments; production qualification ongoing"},{"who":"GTRE","v":"","t":"First indigenous expendable turbojet engine delivered; further engine testing ongoing"}]},"cap":{"util":null,"adds":[{"what":"Six customer-dedicated facilities at Tuniki Bollaram","cap":"44,800 square metres","start":"Commissioned by H1 FY27","capex":"","pot":"Annual revenue run-rate above INR1,300 crores by end of FY28, across installed capacity"},{"what":"Dedicated Baker Hughes oil and gas facility","cap":"","start":"Growth lever from Q4 FY27","capex":"","pot":""},{"what":"Mangampet Phase II","cap":"Land ready for Phase II","start":"After current phase","capex":"","pot":""}],"plan":{"amt":"H1 FY27 capex INR139.3 crores","per":"H1 FY27","fund":"INR80.8 crores QIP money, INR28.6 crores term loan and internal funds"},"turn":""},"decode":{"target":{"m":"Revenue run-rate","lo":"Over INR1,300 crores","hi":"Over INR1,300 crores","p":"By end of FY28"},"margin":{"m":"EBITDA margin","lo":"N/D","hi":"N/D","p":""},"capacity":{"v":"Yes","e":"\"All six customer-dedicated facilities are now commissioned\"; management said installed capacity supports an annual revenue run-rate above INR1,300 crores."},"orders":{"v":"Yes","e":"\"We already have the contracts, we already have the visibility\"; management described customer demand over five to seven years."},"realism":{"v":"Yes","e":"Management linked margin improvement to operating leverage, local sourcing, backward integration and higher throughput from commissioned facilities."}},"risks":"Management cited customer qualification timelines, working-capital requirements, delayed conversion of installed capacity into revenue and uncertainty around engine testing and production schedules.","source":"Azad Engineering Q2 FY27 earnings-call transcript, 7 Nov 2026: prepared remarks pp2–8; Q&A pp9–18. Key Takeaways pp2–3, 5, 7, 13–15; Revenue pp3–4, 8, 15; Profit pp4–6; Pipeline pp3, 7–9, 12, 15; Commitments pp3–5, 7–8, 10–12, 15–18; Metrics pp3–6; Decode pp3–5, 9–10, 13–15; Dilution pp6, 12; Order book pp13–14; Capacity pp2–3, 7–8, 10–12; Glossary pp3–8."}
